  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting the Voices and Engagement of Persons with Lived Experience to Prevent Labor Exploitation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project works to amplify the voices of persons with lived experience to prevent labor exploitation, as well as to provide needed technical support to governments and CSOs as they institutionalize inclusion and meaningful engagements with persons with lived experience. Persons with lived experience&quot; refers to individuals who have directly experienced human trafficking, forced labor, child labor, and/or labor exploitation. These individuals possess first-hand knowledge and understanding of the challenges and impacts associated with such exploitation. Their insights are invaluable for shaping effective prevention, intervention, and support strategies.</narrative>
  </description>
